                <h2>Processing Times from London</h2>
                <p>Typical timelines and factors affecting approval speed</p>
            </div>

            <h3>Typical Processing Timeline</h3>
            <p>From BLS submission to visa approval: <strong>4–12 weeks</strong></p>

            <p>However, timelines vary significantly:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Fast track (4–6 weeks):</strong> Complete applications with all documents, no requests for additional information.</li>
                <li><strong>Standard (6–8 weeks):</strong> Most applications fall into this range.</li>
                <li><strong>Slow track (8–12 weeks):</strong> Applications with incomplete documentation or consulate requests for clarification.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Factors That Speed Up Processing</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Submitting a 100% complete application with all documents on the first attempt</li>
                <li>Clear bank statements showing consistent income for 12+ months</li>
                <li>Proper apostilles and translations (no rejections for formatting)</li>
                <li>Simple employment structure (direct client agreements are clearer than complex contract chains)</li>
                <li>Early submission (applications submitted in off-peak months process faster)</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>Factors That Slow Processing</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Missing or incorrect apostilles</li>
                <li>Poor quality translations or translator not on Spain's official list</li>
                <li>Unclear income documentation (irregular payments, multiple income sources)</li>
                <li>Consulate requesting additional documents (can add 2–4 weeks)</li>
                <li>Applying during peak season (April–July) when consulate is overwhelmed</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>What to Do If Processing Delays Occur</h3>
            <p><strong>After 8 weeks without update:</strong> Contact BLS with your reference number. They can request a status check from the consulate.</p>

            <p><strong>After 12 weeks:</strong> Escalate to the consulate directly. You have the right to know your application status.</p>

            <p><strong>If documents are requested:</strong> The consulate will email you via BLS. Respond within 10–14 days to avoid application rejection.</p>

            <div class="msv__alert msv__alert--warn">
                <span class="msv__alert-icon">⚠️</span>
                <p><strong>Important:</strong> Do not submit a new application or book a new BLS appointment if you're waiting for consulate feedback. Contact the consulate directly first.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

